# The folder tree's right-click menu and the sidebar's Bookmarks section.
#
# A tree menu is about the folder right-clicked, never the file list's selection: every entry
# below names a folder the tab is not showing, and the tab's own folder must be untouched by it.
# Dialogs (New, Properties, What changed) cannot open in a run, so they are not exercised here.

tree .
refresh
assert-row Pictures
tree-menu-run Copy as path on Pictures
assert-status Copied 1 path
assert-path sandbox

# Bookmark, from the tree and from the list; the tree's caption turns into Remove bookmark.
assert-bookmarks none
tree-menu-run Bookmark on Pictures
assert-bookmarks Pictures
select notes.txt
run file.bookmark
assert-bookmarks Pictures | notes.txt
tree-menu-run Remove bookmark on Pictures
assert-bookmarks notes.txt

# A hidden target is listed only while hidden items are shown (dimmed then, like the tree's row).
hidden on
settle 500
select HiddenFolder
run file.bookmark
assert-bookmarks HiddenFolder | notes.txt
shot 01-bookmarks-hidden-shown
hidden off
settle 500
assert-bookmarks notes.txt
shot 02-bookmarks-hidden-left-out

# The tree's Delete asks first, as the list's does: the run puts the confirmation up and answers it.
live-dialogs on
tree-menu-run Delete… on Empty
assert-dialog delete
assert-exists Empty
dialog-press DeleteConfirm
live-dialogs off
assert-missing Empty
assert-path sandbox
# A new tab from the tree opens behind the one in view, as a middle-click does. Spec: ShellViewModel.OpenInNewTab.
tree-menu-run Open in new tab on Documents
assert-path sandbox
assert-tabs 2
tree-menu-run To the right on Pictures
assert-panes 2
assert-path Pictures
shot 03-after-tree-menu
